#6101
The Mud Road~
   A road of trampled mud winds into the camps, lined on both sides with
shelters made of anything at hand: wagon covers, doors, blankets on sticks.
Hollow-eyed faces watch from every opening. A woman holds out an empty bowl
to you without a word.
