#6102
The Northern Tent Rows~
   Tents stand in rows so tight that the guy-ropes cross and tangle. Washing
hangs grey between them. Families from a dozen burned villages huddle
together, speaking dialects from the far west that you have never heard, all
of them describing the same darkness.
