#6103
The Northern Edge of the Camps~
   The tents thin out at the foot of a low rise. At its top stands the grey
stone bulk of the Hospice of the Last Rites, its bell tower dark against the
sky. A line of stretcher-bearers trudges up the slope, and another line,
carrying shrouded shapes, comes down it.
