#6104
The Soup Line~
   A queue hundreds long shuffles toward a row of iron cauldrons, where
soldiers ladle out thin grey broth. When the cauldrons run dry, the soldiers
simply walk away, and the people at the back of the line sit down in the mud
and wait for tomorrow.
